    "title": "Cameron Young's huge net worth and major change encouraged by wife",
    "text": "Cameron Young met his wife, Kelsey Dalition, at Wake Forest University where they both played collegiate golf -Credit:Getty Images (Getty Images)Cameron Young met his wife, Kelsey Dalition, at Wake Forest University where they both played collegiate golf -Credit:Getty Images (Getty Images)Cameron Young competed in his first Ryder Cup last year and did so riding the momentum of finally securing his first PGA Tour win at the Wyndham Championship.Young's selection after receiving a captain's pick from Keegan Bradley represented another sign of the 28-year-old's continued rise on the PGA Tour. And he has picked up where he left off in 2026, fighting Matt Fitzpatrick, who's wife made a big decision as they faced an awkward scenario, for the win in a dramatic finale at The PLAYERS Championship.His breakthrough campaign featured his inaugural victory, combining substantial prize money with an expanding presence away from competition. Beyond the course, his journey is characterized by both financial achievement and the understated yet meaningful backing of his wife, Kelsey Dalition, who has even shaped how he carries himself at golf's premier events.• Matt Fitzpatrick was 'surprised' by Ludvig Aberg personality when he first met him• PGA Tour rookie self-taught from YouTube about to win life-changing money at The PlayersWhat is Cameron Young's net worth?As of 2025, Cameron Young's net worth is projected to be approximately $17 to $18 million.This estimate captures his recent emergence, including his maiden PGA Tour triumph at the Wyndham Championship in early August 2025, where he controlled the field and claimed a considerable winner's check of nearly $1.5 million.Beyond his tournament prizes, his career earnings, including majors, reach $28.8 million according to Spotrac, placing him 108th on the all-time PGA Tour money list. Additional income streams include endorsement deals - he has served as a brand ambassador for firms like Peter Millar and iCapital, among others - further supplementing his earnings off the fairways.Who is Cameron Young's wife?Cameron Young's Wife Young is married to Kelsey Dalition, an exceptionally private person who seldom appears on social media and prefers to keep her personal life out of the spotlight. The couple married in an intimate ceremony in 2021, shortly after Young turned professional, with his former college teammate and caddie, Scott McKean, acting as best man.Cameron Young used to have a very different lookKelsey is believed to be a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) and played collegiate golf at Wake Forest University. Though she keeps a low profile, she regularly attends his tournaments in a supportive capacity, including The Masters Par-3 Contest and the 2025 Genesis Invitational, often with their children by her side.The family resides in Jupiter, Florida, having purchased a home there in 2022 after initially living with Young's parents during the early stages of their relationship. They have three children together, including their eldest, Henry, who was born in 2022.Young's new look wife encouragedOne notable instance that highlighted Kelsey Dalition's subtle influence occurred ahead of the 2023 PGA Championship at Oak Hill Country Club. Known for his distinctive facial hair, Cameron arrived at the tournament clean-shaven, a dramatic change he credited to his wife's suggestion.As he explained, \"Honestly, my wife just kind of said, why don't you shave... I haven't been clean‐shaven probably since our first son was born.\"",
